> > Hi Young,
> > Thank you for the info, I've gotten it to work with a loss of zero. However, I'm having trouble editing the function to take the probabilities as an argument. The code I have created, based on your suggested edits of the ra_noLA function, seems to run, but I am getting an warning saying "Stan model 'ra_noLA_edit' does not contain samples, and it doesn't look the model finished running. I've attached my version of the ra_noLA function and the sample data I edited to see if you might have an idea where I'm going wrong.
